==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|harmles}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*hearmlēas}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*harmalausaz||without harm; harmless}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|harm|less}}.

Cognate with {{cog|de|harmlos||harmless}}, {{cog|da|harmløs||harlmess}}, {{cog|sv|harmlös||harmless}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈhɑɹmləs/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈhɑːmləs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-harmless.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[incapable|Incapable]] of causing [[harm]] or [[danger]]; [[safe]].
# Not [[intend]]ed to harm; [[inoffensive]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=w:Ben Travers
|chapter=5|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1521052W A Cuckoo in the Nest]
|passage=The most rapid and most seductive transition in all human nature is that which attends the palliation of a ravenous appetite.{{...}}Can those '''harmless''' but refined fellow-diners be the selfish cads whose gluttony and personal appearance so raised your contemptuous wrath on your arrival?}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[unharmed|Unharmed]].

